# Initial Project Setup Guidelines

> file_patterns: ["*.py", "setup.py", "requirements.txt"]
> description: Guidelines for initial project setup and structure

## Basic Framework Setup
Guidelines for initial development:
- Implement minimum viable feature set
- Establish clear module boundaries
- Define core interfaces and data structures

### Code Quality Baseline
> required: true

Essential quality requirements:
- Complete type annotations
- Standard docstrings
- Basic unit tests
- Unified code style

### Configuration Setup
Required configuration elements:
- Environment variable configuration
- Logging system setup
- Dependency version management
- Development environment setup

## Design Pattern Implementation

### Processor Pattern
Guidelines for business logic organization:
- Business logic layer for flow orchestration only
- Complex logic delegated to processors
- Base processors independently testable

### Workspace Management
Guidelines for workspace handling:
- Share context through md_info
- Ensure workspace isolation for safety
- Avoid direct original file modification

### Basic Patterns
Common design patterns to consider:
- Factory pattern for object creation
- Strategy pattern for algorithm variants
- Observer pattern for event handling
- Decorator pattern for feature extension

## Project Initialization

### Environment Setup
> required: true

Initial environment requirements:
- Virtual environment creation
- Dependencies installation
- Environment variable configuration
- Development tools setup

### Version Control Setup
> required: true

Initial repository setup:
- Git initialization
- .gitignore configuration
- Branch strategy setup
- Commit message guidelines

### Documentation Setup
Initial documentation requirements:
- README.md creation
- API documentation structure
- Development guide setup
- Contribution guidelines

## Validation Requirements
- Project structure must follow standards
- All required files must be present
- Initial tests must pass
- Documentation must be complete 